--TEST--
All three `Core\Topic` members refuse an empty name, and they agree on the sentence rather than each having grown its own — `rule:core-classes/topic`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The empty name is the one no publisher can mean and no subscriber can be
// reached by, and the class refuses it at every door. What this case asks is
// not what each member answered -- a sibling case already prints two of those
// -- but whether the three *agree*: one sentence with only the member's own
// name in it. A member that grew its own wording, or that answered a count of
// nobody instead of refusing, still looks right on its own line and fails
// here.
var $tail = " needs a topic name and was given an empty one";

var $fromSubscribe = "";
try {
    Core\Topic::subscribe("");
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    $fromSubscribe = $refused->message;
}

var $fromPublish = "";
try {
    Core\Topic::publish("", "anything");
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    $fromPublish = $refused->message;
}

var $fromUnsubscribe = "";
try {
    Core\Topic::unsubscribe("");
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    $fromUnsubscribe = $refused->message;
}

if ($fromSubscribe == "`Core\\Topic::subscribe`" . $tail) {
    echo "subscribe agrees\n";
} else {
    echo $fromSubscribe, "\n";
}

if ($fromPublish == "`Core\\Topic::publish`" . $tail) {
    echo "publish agrees\n";
} else {
    echo $fromPublish, "\n";
}

if ($fromUnsubscribe == "`Core\\Topic::unsubscribe`" . $tail) {
    echo "unsubscribe agrees\n";
} else {
    echo $fromUnsubscribe, "\n";
}

// The name is the first thing every one of them reads. `publish` has no second
// question to ask -- it is not on a connection and does not care -- so the
// empty name is the whole of what it can refuse, and it refuses it before the
// value is so much as copied.
try {
    Core\Topic::publish("", new Credential());
    echo "published\n";
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}

class Credential {
    public secret string $token = "s3cr3t";
}
--EXPECT--
subscribe agrees
publish agrees
unsubscribe agrees
`Core\Topic::publish` needs a topic name and was given an empty one
